3e77ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-123278" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t+1},\\,t-3⟩,$ $|r(6)|=$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(6) & =⟨\\sqrt{6+1},\\,6-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{7},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(6)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{7})}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7+9} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "1e783eb9-a681-5eba-aacc-969cf4aaad76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "caacf1bc-fd87-52e7-a970-e14f936e68d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316656/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-316656/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-2/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "61eee858-9a01-5916-a798-6dae9f065b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e87432d-f293-5f0a-97cd-73a0d11f52b5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316656/field-2/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-316656/field-2/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-3/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "0db6309b-88a7-5654-a2cc-a9af8a9e88e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "28148e31-6f17-509e-82a6-3b63ae1ce93d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316656/field-3/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-316656/field-3/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-4/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer/id #uuid "c5cc0e13-1cd7-5e8d-b698-eb812c0cbabe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1338656-9fbd-550f-a4c6-448c80dd2aec" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316656/field-4/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer-field/choices ["q-316656/field-4/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316656" :question/id #uuid "ffd0c8c4-243f-527a-8c14-0416289f3f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-316656" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5,{x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-5)({x}^{2}-x(-1-2\\text{i})-x(-1+2\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-5)({x}^{2}+2x+5) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+5x-5{x}^{2}-10x-25) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5x-25) & = \\\\ -4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316656/field-1" "q-316656/field-2" "q-316656/field-3" "q-316656/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979/selection/ac07ebd7a4946b05c45360eea758a877ebf5c34730ae94039788b0b6df181377" :answer/id #uuid "aeff69f1-6949-54b0-b1a7-ea39fe4aabfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979/selection/14b1ad3e3f9f098e09552d0ecaf05b863ff1e5eaff41bcebc12514462c8366c4" :answer/id #uuid "da77c455-02e5-50bd-810e-e340a636b71c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{11\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979/selection/a105e9b0c17a9ac74a2869bbeee0e5992f84aa361472bd6f26ca6a056bdcbeef" :answer/id #uuid "c4a7b28b-9e88-5e6b-9c0f-2372746f313b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979/selection/bba1e8e2b57e61e8c120ac6fa53dd920cdcf157c79db230e9280e132bd82ac60" :answer/id #uuid "25e3fa19-33cc-54f8-ae33-526b77479b45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{11\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979/selection/322a3cc4d7de150f2e935f30c255050ac9cbac134474468d7b2c72efa8efb67f" :answer/id #uuid "3da8bb85-6076-5ecf-8269-02ce64b53c97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "313e1229-1616-5b11-a259-8de3d7c72c67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71979/selection/bba1e8e2b57e61e8c120ac6fa53dd920cdcf157c79db230e9280e132bd82ac60" :answer-field/choices ["q-71979/selection/ac07ebd7a4946b05c45360eea758a877ebf5c34730ae94039788b0b6df181377" "q-71979/selection/14b1ad3e3f9f098e09552d0ecaf05b863ff1e5eaff41bcebc12514462c8366c4" "q-71979/selection/a105e9b0c17a9ac74a2869bbeee0e5992f84aa361472bd6f26ca6a056bdcbeef" "q-71979/selection/bba1e8e2b57e61e8c120ac6fa53dd920cdcf157c79db230e9280e132bd82ac60" "q-71979/selection/322a3cc4d7de150f2e935f30c255050ac9cbac134474468d7b2c72efa8efb67f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71979" :question/id #uuid "ce405741-9ecc-5ff1-a4c2-a25ead99ec54" :question/math-academy-id "q-71979" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=3-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{11\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/requires-calculator true :question/answer-fields ["q-71979/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71979"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613/selection/4512ce45648cf728c97a513e88e73eaba03db6fbed435f441fed92e911aaa4d3" :answer/id #uuid "ef99a009-6ed9-516b-9f51-a639fc401277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{211}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613/selection/e0bbd50c335374903328ed689b33aff7962423802dfbf7fae7297cfe90af6f0d" :answer/id #uuid "2f124855-4137-5692-a3f2-69212423fd83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{422}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613/selection/53b9af06220e71321e503a4f3e6765adc3e5f6015c8c7280848b20265c466aa1" :answer/id #uuid "28f896fe-615c-5693-99e7-b6591110f4c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{96}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613/selection/2ea175975ab021a5d2fc5aa9eef081ce8ef32114e4a26ead5425628dcbb64240" :answer/id #uuid "36ab5a53-ee6a-55d4-891a-4100dfe7b2f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{484}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613/selection/b336641abcb999c21c9e53c96c83b284fdf2bf3a3de0d87fa53f648928975e27" :answer/id #uuid "f4b80bb4-7776-5793-95cb-0a1dff265265" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a058c696-13e3-591e-a553-6de7c76888cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49613/selection/e0bbd50c335374903328ed689b33aff7962423802dfbf7fae7297cfe90af6f0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-49613/selection/4512ce45648cf728c97a513e88e73eaba03db6fbed435f441fed92e911aaa4d3" "q-49613/selection/e0bbd50c335374903328ed689b33aff7962423802dfbf7fae7297cfe90af6f0d" "q-49613/selection/53b9af06220e71321e503a4f3e6765adc3e5f6015c8c7280848b20265c466aa1" "q-49613/selection/2ea175975ab021a5d2fc5aa9eef081ce8ef32114e4a26ead5425628dcbb64240" "q-49613/selection/b336641abcb999c21c9e53c96c83b284fdf2bf3a3de0d87fa53f648928975e27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49613" :question/id #uuid "b67dc0a6-51f8-5dfe-a448-7ac0ef9d5e96" :question/math-academy-id "q-49613" :question/problem "Evaluate the definite integral ${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\sqrt{{(5x-6)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =5x-6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =5\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5x-6.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ u & 4 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\sqrt{{(5x-6)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{4}^{9}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}|}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}({9}^{5/2}-{4}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}(({3}^{2})^{5/2}-({2}^{2})^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}({3}^{5}-{2}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}(243-32) \\\\  & =\\frac{422}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49613/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dcde3b5-5cdf-5266-9392-0835053a7ded"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6ad18234-c2f1-5de7-8b86-0489a830a837" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb8d367-be22-5532-b11b-b266c6ffd1d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276950/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-276950/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "e0717a19-164f-51e4-8032-7b3d3f142c0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f01ef642-7656-5c8c-af96-d141a5faa304" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276950/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-276950/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "07676991-05b9-5258-a67e-8d3deef9d373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac5f18b9-9ac7-5341-94e3-123cfdb29d0f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276950/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-276950/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276950" :question/id #uuid "30a43708-f16f-596d-8fb5-c42ef7a03f99" :question/math-academy-id "q-276950" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-x)+1\\le \\operatorname{log}⁡(x+9).$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\le \\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We use each side of the inequality as an exponent of $10.$ This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-x)+1} & \\le {10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+9)} \\\\ {10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-x)}\\cdot {10}^{1} & \\le {10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+9)} \\\\ (2-x)\\cdot 10 & \\le x+9 \\\\ 20-10x & \\le x+9 \\\\ -11x & \\le -11 \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the logarithms in the original inequality. To find the domain of the logarithms, we recall that the argument of the logarithm must be positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & <2 \\\\ x+9 & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & >-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x\\ge 1,$ which can be expressed as $[1,\\infty ).$ Additionally, the domains of the logarithms are $x<2$ and $x>-11,$ which can be expressed as $(-\\infty ,2)$ and $(-11,\\infty )$ respectively. To find the solutions that are in the domains of the logarithms, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n[1,\\infty )\\cap (-\\infty ,2)\\cap (-9,\\infty )=[1,2)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in [1,2),$ which can also be written as $1\\le x<2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-276950/field-1" "q-276950/field-2" "q-276950/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "106dce79-251c-52b2-adc7-9fd2b59b9b83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276950"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129219/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d8547ab0-a3ca-54f8-b924-8ef28c4e00a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129219/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "fd1970cb-22e3-5928-b7b7-06ef9ca9a93c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129219/selection/6a8