the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,4]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,4].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-2,4)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129219/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
